<com:TContent ID="body" >

<h1>TTextBox</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TTextBox" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TTextBox</tt> displays a text box on a Web page. The content in the text box is determined by the <tt>Text</tt> property. The <tt>TextMode</tt> property selects the kind of input the control renders. The <tt>Rows</tt> and <tt>Columns</tt> properties size the box. If <tt>AutoPostBack</tt> is true, changing the content in the text box and then moving the focus out of it will cause postback action.
</p>
<h2>Input modes</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TextMode</tt> takes one of sixteen values. It defaults to <tt>SingleLine</tt>. The
first three modes are the original ones.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Mode</th><th>Renders</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>SingleLine</tt></td>
	<td><tt>&lt;input type="text"&gt;</tt></td>
	<td>The default mode.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>MultiLine</tt></td>
	<td><tt>&lt;textarea&gt;</tt></td>
	<td><tt>Rows</tt> and <tt>Columns</tt> set its size. <tt>Wrap</tt> controls line wrapping.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Password</tt></td>
	<td><tt>&lt;input type="password"&gt;</tt></td>
	<td>The control discards the value on postback unless <tt>PersistPassword</tt> is true.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<h3>HTML5 input modes</h3>
<com:SinceVersion Version="4.0.0" />

<p class="block-content">
Thirteen further modes render the HTML5 input types. Each mode writes its own
<tt>type</tt> attribute. A browser that does not implement a type renders a plain text
field instead, so the server still receives a string and <tt>Text</tt> still holds it.
Validation of the value remains the application's job.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Mode</th><th>Renders</th></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Color</tt></td><td><tt>type="color"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Date</tt></td><td><tt>type="date"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Datetime</tt></td><td><tt>type="datetime"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>DatetimeLocal</tt></td><td><tt>type="datetime-local"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Email</tt></td><td><tt>type="email"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Month</tt></td><td><tt>type="month"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Number</tt></td><td><tt>type="number"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Range</tt></td><td><tt>type="range"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Search</tt></td><td><tt>type="search"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Tel</tt></td><td><tt>type="tel"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Time</tt></td><td><tt>type="time"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Url</tt></td><td><tt>type="url"</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>Week</tt></td><td><tt>type="week"</tt></td></tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
The HTML standard withdrew the <tt>datetime</tt> type. Browsers render the
<tt>Datetime</tt> mode as a plain text field. Use <tt>DatetimeLocal</tt> for a date and
time entry.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TTextBox TextMode="Email" /&gt;
&lt;com:TTextBox TextMode="Number" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>Reading the input safely</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>Text</tt> returns what the user typed. A page that writes that value back into its
output without escaping it opens a cross-site scripting hole. <tt>SafeText</tt> returns
the same value with scripting removed. <tt>TTextBox</tt> produces it by running
<tt>Text</tt> through HTML Purifier.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$this-&gt;Result-&gt;Text = $this-&gt;Input-&gt;SafeText;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h3>Purifier configuration</h3>
<com:SinceVersion Version="4.0.0" />

<p class="block-content">
The <tt>Config</tt> property holds an <tt>HTMLPurifier_Config</tt> object that governs
what <tt>SafeText</tt> keeps. Leaving it unset gives the default configuration, which
caches its serialized definitions under the application's <tt>runtime/htmlpurifier</tt>
directory. That directory must be writable by the web server.
</p>

<h2>Trimming input</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>AutoTrim</tt> defaults to false. Setting it to true makes the control strip leading
and trailing whitespace from the posted value before it reaches <tt>Text</tt>. The trim
happens while the control loads post data, so a validator sees the trimmed value.
</p>

